CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260527T142548Z
DESCRIPTION:On October 3 and 4\, the Program in American Grand Strategy wi
 ll hold our annual staff ride - this year to Yorktown\, Virginia\, site o
 f the final major campaign of the American Revolutionary War.\n\n2026 mar
 ks the 250th anniversary of American independence\, and the Yorktown camp
 aign of 1781 is the hinge on which that independence turned. Without Wash
 ington and Rochambeau's audacious march south\, without the French fleet'
 s decisive victory at the Battle of the Capes\, and without the siege tha
 t forced Cornwallis's surrender\, there might be no United States. There 
 is no better moment to walk this ground.\n\nA staff ride is a hands-on ed
 ucational experience where participants walk the terrain of a battle or c
 ampaign. Participants will visit the battlefield and deliver a presentati
 on from the perspective of an individual involved in the Yorktown Campaig
 n - drawn from a cast of historical figures that includes American comman
 ders\, French allies\, British generals and ministers\, a private soldier
 \, a camp follower\, and an enslaved man who escaped to the British lines
  in search of the freedom the Revolution promised but did not yet deliver
 .\n\nStudents are encouraged to apply regardless of program of study\, ye
 ar\, or prior involvement with AGS. We are looking for students intereste
 d in and willing to participate in an exciting learning exercise on the A
 merican Revolution\, focusing on the Yorktown Campaign of 1781. No specif
 ic expertise is required.\n\nAGS will cover all travel and lodging costs 
 for participants\, along with meals. Students will be responsible for any
  recreational expenses outside of the staff ride's program.
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T200000
