CREATED:20260909T173105Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a second free public event with visiting artist Ke
 nya (Robinson)\, following her October 3 performance\, "Fluid Master."\n\
 nUsing the first edition of TURBO TAROT\, Kenya explores the integrated s
 ystems of a passenger vehicle through the symbolic framework of the tarot
 . Blending automotive maintenance\, philosophy\, and live tarot readings\
 , participants will examine engines\, fluids\, tools\, and suspension as 
 interconnected systems that reveal broader ideas about labor\, care\, tra
 nsformation\, and resilience.\n\nNo automotive knowledge or tarot experie
 nce is required. Participants will engage with an unconventional mix of a
 utomotive knowledge\, philosophy\, and live tarot readings led by Kenya f
 rom the first edition of TURBO TAROT.\n\nThe four suits of TURBO TAROT co
 rrespond to the integrated systems of a passenger vehicle:\n\nFire / Wand
 s: Engine\, Ignition & Electrical Systems\nWater / Cups: Fluids & Hydraul
 ic Systems\nAir / Swords: Tools & Fasteners\nEarth / Pentacles: Brakes & 
 Suspension\n\nSpace is limited to 25 - 30 people\, so please register to 
 reserve your spot here: https://rsvp.duke.edu/event/a7d45621-7803-4dde-b4
 cb-df0d6b3ae83a/summary\n\nTURBO TAROT is a new artist-directed project t
 hat uses generative AI as one component of an iterative visualization and
  production process. Kenya developed the project's conceptual framework\,
  automotive-to-tarot correspondences\, visual system\, imagery\, and indi
 vidual card concepts\, using AI tools as one component of the artistic pr
 ocess.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20261001T155808Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T100000
