CREATED:20261001T170641Z
DESCRIPTION:Eight hundred years after his death\, St. Francis of Assisi re
 mains one of the most recognizable and beloved figures in Christian histo
 ry. But the real Francis was far more interesting-and challenging-than th
 e gentle saint surrounded by birds and animals that we often imagine. \n\
 nJoin Pastor Ryan for a conversation about Francis's remarkable life\, hi
 s embrace of poverty and simplicity\, his encounters across boundaries\, 
 his sense of kinship with all creation\, and the movement he inspired. Al
 ong the way\, we'll ask what this 13th-century saint might still have to 
 teach the Church-and us-800 years later.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261001T170919Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T094500
