  Serena
CREATED:20260716T122056Z
DESCRIPTION:The North Carolina Jewish Studies Seminar welcomes Ayelet Brin
 n\, Assistant Professor at Hebrew Union College's Skirball (Los Angeles) 
 Campus.  Her research focuses on American Jewish history\, gender\, Yiddi
 sh studies\, and popular culture. \n\nBrinn holds a PhD in history from t
 he University of Pennsylvania and master's degrees in history and library
  science from Indiana University.   She was previously assistant professo
 r of modern Jewish history and associate director of the Greenberg Center
  for Judaic Studies at the University of Hartford and has held fellowship
 s at the Hadassah-Brandeis Institute\, the Katz Center for Advanced Judai
 c Studies at the University of Pennsylvania\, and at Fordham University a
 nd Columbia University.\n\nHer first book\, A Revolution in Type: Gender 
 and the Making of the American Yiddish Press\, was published by New York 
 University Press in November 2023 and received the the Association for Je
 wish Studies' 2025 Jordan Schnitzer Award in Modern Jewish History & Cult
 ure: Africa\, Americas\, Asia\, & Oceania.  She had also been awarded a s
 ummer fellowship from the National Endowment for the Humanities. Brinn is
  currently writing a second book\, which will examine U.S. censorship and
  surveillance of the Yiddish press during World War I and the first Red S
 care. She has also published articles in such prestigious journals as Stu
 dies in American Jewish Literature and American Jewish History on topics 
 that include Jewish American journalism during the beginning of the 20th 
 century and female journalists in the American Yiddish press.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260804T124004Z
