CREATED:20260916T130345Z
DESCRIPTION:Led by staff from Duke University Libraries\, this online Resp
 onsible Conduct of Research session for new graduate students serves as a
 n introduction to library resources as well as an overview of essential p
 ractices and topics in ethical\, responsible research in the arts & human
 ities. Topics include:\n\n\n•    using library databases and finding mate
 rials\,\n•    special collections and rare book/manuscript research\,\n• 
    copyright and author's rights\,\n•    citation and attribution\,\n•   
  practices in the digital humanities\,\n•    research impact and metrics\
 ,\n•    research data management\,\n•    scholarly networks and communiti
 es.\n\nThis workshop has been approved for two hours of RCR credit and is
  intended for new graduate students in the arts & humanities.\n\nZoom inf
 ormation will be sent via email to registered attendees the day before th
 e session.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260916T130345Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T100000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260916T130345Z
