CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a0183a7-83184018-0184-87170e31-00006277:Hinz\, Nic
 olle
CREATED:20260921T173146Z
DESCRIPTION:One of the hallmarks of adaptive matter is the ability to sens
 e and respond to the environment. How can we engineer soft matter systems
  to exhibit such behavior? In this talk\, I will present our recent findi
 ngs on systems driven by centimeter-scale actuators (electric motors) and
  nanometer-scale actuators (myosin motors)\, using methods from control t
 heory to either design function or probe system properties. Such control-
 theoretical approaches are often exploited in engineering applications. I
  will instead emphasize how control in active and robotic systems can hel
 p physicists better understand information processing\, orchestration of 
 function\, and adaptability in living systems.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260921T173146Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T173146Z
