CREATED:20260226T141817Z
DESCRIPTION:An "Independent Thinkers" Conversation with U.S. Rep Jake Auch
 incloss hosted by Frank Bruni\, Duke professor and New York Times columni
 st\n\nHas the Democratic Party learned the lessons of its 2024 defeats\, 
 in terms of not just the contests this November but the future in general
 ? How can Democrats escape Republicans' caricatures of them and promote i
 deas that transcend partisanship and unite diverse people?\n\nPlease join
  Frank Bruni for a probing conversation - part of his "Independent Thinke
 rs" series of events - with U.S. Representative Jake Auchincloss\, a risi
 ng Democratic star and one of his party's least predictable and most thou
 ghtful leaders.\n\nAuchincloss\, 38\, is in his third term in Congress\, 
 representing the 4th Congressional District in Massachusetts. He's the in
 augural chair of Majority Democrats\, a group of lawmakers insistent that
  the party devote less energy to deriding President Trump and more to dev
 eloping an agenda that reaches beyond its base. He's a graduate of Harvar
 d and M.I.T. and a combat veteran who served as an active-duty Marine fro
 m 2010 to 2015.\n\nFrank Bruni teaches at Duke's Sanford School of Public
  Policy as part of the DeWitt Wallace Center for Media and Democracy. He'
 s also a longtime writer for The New York Times and the author of five be
 stselling books.\n\nFrank's "Independent Thinkers" conversations with pub
 lic figures who defy reductive political labels are part of the Provost's
  Initiative on Pluralism\, Free Inquiry and Belonging.
DURATION:PT1H15M
DTSTAMP:20261002T150246Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T180000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T150246Z
